                            "derivation": "Minimum corner radius the 5.0 x 1.0 mm rectangular copper wire (IEC 60317, grade 1, outer width 5.085000 mm per MKF) can be wound around ON EDGE. IEC 60317-0-2 Table 6 (mandrel winding, rectangular copper, width <= 10 mm): mandrel = 4 x conductor width = 4 x 5.000 mm = 20.000 mm. IEC 60851-3 5.1.1 winds the wire on the mandrel, so the minimum centreline bend radius is mandrel/2 + outer width/2 = 10.000 + 2.5425 = 12.542500 mm (MKF WireBend::get_minimum_bend_radius, FLEXIBILITY, EDGEWISE). The turn centreline stands 2.550000 mm off the former face (half the wire's declared 5.1 mm outer width; MKF Coil standoff). columnCornerRadius = 12.542500 mm - 2.550000 mm = 9.992500 mm, the minimum MKF's ABT #1290 check accepts; no margin added. Computed with MKF d1ee5b10 against MAS b294ba6."
