                                "processedDescription.columnDepth"
                            ],
                            "derivation": "Core column (MKF processed E 70/33/32, 2 stacks): width F = 21.650000 mm, depth 2 x C = 63.200000 mm, both nominal, sharp corners (MAS gives the E column no corner radius). t_q = 2.349681 mm is the column-wall thickness MKF Bobbin::create_quick_bobbin interpolates for this core window from the MAS bobbin catalogue, taken as the thinnest wall a moulded former of this size is shown to have. With a corner radius R on the outer winding surface and a square bore on the core column, the plastic between the core's corner and the rounded surface, measured on the diagonal, is R - sqrt(2) x (R - t). Requiring it to be at least t_q gives t >= R x (1 - 1/sqrt(2)) + t_q/sqrt(2) = 4.588211 mm, taken up to the next nanometre: columnThickness = 4.588211 mm. columnWidth = F/2 + t = 15.413211 mm; columnDepth = (2 x C)/2 + t = 36.188211 mm (MKF stores both as half-dimensions of the outer winding surface). R / half the smaller outer side = 0.6483 < 1, so the column stays a rectangle with rounded corners (10.841422 mm flat on the narrow face)."
